        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(extensions): burn down Discord and Slack dead exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe dead-export ratchet prevents new unused exports, but Discord and Slack still carried 205 grandfathered entries. This burns down 103 confirmed-dead exports without touching the shipped plugin SDK or intentional lazy/runtime and test seams.\n\nRelated: #105736\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Audited all 133 Discord and 72 Slack baseline entries against direct imports, barrel imports, tests, string-keyed access, and `*.runtime.ts` lazy bridges.\n- Removed 77 Discord and 26 Slack entries: redundant barrels, private types/constants, unused testing aliases, and declarations used only by their own dead tests.\n- Retargeted surviving tests to canonical owner modules instead of preserving dead re-export barrels.\n- Preserved explicit testing objects, runtime bridges, and public/plugin SDK contracts.\n- Ratcheted three touched large-file LOC counters downward.\n- Updated the Discord doctor expectation for the inherited streaming shape now produced by #105808; runtime code is unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. The unused-export baseline drops from 5,510 to 5,407 lines (103 entries), while production TypeScript shrinks by a net 121 lines.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Testbox `tbx_01kxcvabb6sh4bh99d3xnp91sh` / Actions run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29223733692\n- `pnpm test extensions/discord`: 171 files, 2,032 tests passed\n- `pnpm test extensions/slack`: 120 files, 1,872 tests passed\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports`: baseline matched 5,399 entries\n- `pnpm format:check`\n- `pnpm build`\n- `pnpm check:changed`: branch-owned gates passed through production extension typecheck; the extension test typecheck then hit the unrelated QA-Lab fixture mismatch fixed on current `main` by #105983\n- Fresh whole-branch autoreview after the current-main refresh: no accepted/actionable findings; patch correct (0.96)\n",
